2. Limited permission for artifact evaluation

Subject to the conditions below, CESAR/CISSA grants members of the Technical
Artifact Committee (CTA), reviewers, and authorized organizers of SBSeg 2026 a
limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable, and royalty-free
permission to access, copy as technically necessary, install, execute, and
inspect the Artifact solely for:

  a. evaluating the artifact associated with the paper "Beyond Aggregate
     Accuracy: Kill Chain-Aware Evaluation of IoMT Intrusion Detection
     Models"; and
  b. verifying the scientific claims reported in that paper during the SBSeg
     2026 artifact-evaluation process.

This permission includes execution in local machines, virtual machines, and
containers controlled by the authorized evaluator. Reasonable internal notes
and evaluation reports may be created for the confidential review process.

3. Restrictions

Except with prior written authorization from CESAR/CISSA, recipients may not:

  a. use the Artifact for commercial, production, operational, consulting,
